      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. that's a good start but the parser is still flagging it as \"low density\" for the sub-sections. it's basically complaining that there aren't enough specific data points to validate every single subsystem.\n\ncan you expand this significantly? we need detailed breakdowns for the voltage rails, clock frequencies per core cluster, thermal sensor tolerances, and power efficiency metrics across different load states. just make sure you pack in a massive amount of specific numeric values and percentages for every category so the parser treats it as a complete, high-density spec. try to cover as many granular specs as possible.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
